Check ADF (or a Markdown conversion) without writing output

Usage: adf validate [OPTIONS] [INPUT]

Arguments:
  [INPUT]
          Input file, or `-` for stdin (the default)

Options:
      --from <FROM>
          Input format; auto: ADF when the input is a JSON object, else Markdown

          Possible values:
          - auto: ADF when the input starts with `{`, Markdown otherwise
          - md:   A dry run of `adf convert`
          - adf:  Check an ADF document or envelope
          
          [default: auto]

  -e, --envelope <ENVELOPE>
          Wrap the document for an API (Markdown input only; ADF input is detected)

          Possible values:
          - doc:              The bare document
          - jira-comment:     {"body": DOC}
          - jira-description: {"fields": {"description": DOC}}
          - jira-field:       {"fields": {"<NAME>": DOC}} (needs --field NAME)
          - confluence:       {"representation": "atlas_doc_format", "value": "<DOC as a JSON
            string>"}

      --field <NAME>
          Field name: for -e jira-field, or which `fields` entry to read from ADF input (default
          description)

  -t, --target <TARGET>
          Product whose rules to check; auto: confluence for Confluence envelopes, else jira

          Possible values:
          - auto:       Follow the envelope
          - jira:       Jira Cloud
          - confluence: Confluence Cloud
          
          [default: auto]

      --strict
          Treat warnings as failures (E_LOSSY, exit 5)

      --json
          Write a JSON report to stdout (schemas/validate-report.v1.json)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Markdown options:
      --softbreak <MODE>
          What a newline inside a paragraph becomes

          Possible values:
          - space:     A space (CommonMark)
          - hardbreak: A hardBreak node (as GitHub comments render it)
          
          [default: space]

      --html <POLICY>
          What happens to HTML without an ADF equivalent

          Possible values:
          - text:  Keep it as literal text (W_HTML_AS_TEXT)
          - drop:  Remove it (W_HTML_DROPPED)
          - error: Fail with E_LOSSY
          
          [default: text]

      --images <POLICY>
          What happens to images

          Possible values:
          - link:     A link to the image (W_IMAGE_AS_LINK)
          - external: An external mediaSingle (Jira rendering unverified)
          - drop:     Remove it (W_IMAGE_DROPPED)
          
          [default: link]

      --extensions <LIST>
          ADF extensions to recognise: all, none, or a comma-separated list
          (alerts,details,cells,raw-adf,mention,status,date,emoji,card)
          
          [default: all]

Global options:
      --error-format <FORMAT>
          How diagnostics are printed on stderr [default: auto] [env: ADF_ERROR_FORMAT]

          Possible values:
          - auto: Text on a terminal, JSON lines otherwise
          - text: `file:line:col: severity[CODE]: message`
          - json: One JSON object per line (schemas/diagnostic.v1.json)

  -q, --quiet
          Do not print warnings (errors are always printed; exit codes are unchanged)

      --no-color
          Never use colour (also: the NO_COLOR environment variable)
